returned as exact strings; larger ones become doubles. \code{Infinity}, \code{-Infinity} and \code{NaN} become \code{Inf}, \code{-Inf} and \code{NaN}.
}

\section{Limitations}{

R strings cannot contain the NUL character, so strings that contain \verb{\\0},
\verb{\\x00} or \verb{\\u0000} raise an error. Duplicate keys in an object are all kept,
as in jsonlite (the specification leaves this to implementations).
